\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {71}{\ignorespaces Discrete $\hat  \zeta $-slices of the reconstructed amplitudes $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle A$}\mathaccent "0365{A}^{[x]\text  {Re}}_{2B}$ and $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle A$}\mathaccent "0365{A}^{[x]\text  {Im}}_{2B}$ and the unpolarized and Sivers TMD combinations $\tilde  f_1^{(0)}=2\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle A$}\mathaccent "0365{A}^{[x]}_{2B}$ and $\tilde  f_{1T}^{\perp (1)}=-2\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle A$}\mathaccent "0365{A}^{[x]\text  {Re}}_{12B}$, plotted against both $x$ and $1/\hat  \zeta $ at fixed transverse separation $|b_T| = 3a \approx 0.34$ fm. Each ribbon corresponds to one of the four simulated momenta $P_L = -1,-2,-3,-4$ (equivalently $1/\hat  \zeta = 11.02,\ 3.40,\ 1.85,\ 1.27$). The systematic drift of every panel with $1/\hat  \zeta $ motivates the extrapolation to the light-cone limit $\hat  \zeta \to \infty $ performed below.\relax }}{158}{figure.caption.103}\protected@file@percent }
